            "id": "AID-I-003",
            "name": "Quarantine & Throttling of AI Interactions",
            "description": "Contain suspicious AI activity by degrading, rate-limiting, quarantining, or blocking the specific identity, session, tenant, agent instance, resource budget, or high-risk action that is creating risk.<br/><br/><strong>Control families:</strong> child controls separate detection-driven quarantine and safe mode, identity/session/API throttling, resource-token-spend budget throttling, and per-action containment before side effects. This split reflects real engineering ownership: SecOps/SOAR, API gateway, platform/FinOps, and agent orchestration teams.",
            "scopeBoundary": {
              "responsibility": "Owns reversible response-time containment after a detection, policy, health, trust-state, or budget signal crosses a containment threshold. It translates existing findings into bounded quarantine, degradation, rate limiting, budget throttling, or per-action enforcement; it does not compute the signal or perform durable eviction.",
              "relatedTechniques": [
                {
                  "id": "AID-E-002",
                  "comparison": "AID-I-003 applies reversible quarantine, safe mode, throttling, or action containment; AID-E-002 revokes execution leases and terminates confirmed-compromised runtime processes, jobs, pods, and containers.\nUse this family for bounded containment while investigation or recovery proceeds, and E-002 when the incident decision requires authoritative live-execution eviction."
                },
                {
                  "id": "AID-I-005",
                  "comparison": "AID-I-003 contains a scoped identity, session, tenant, agent, budget, or action; AID-I-005 applies a last-resort system-wide or tenant-wide halt or severe restriction.\nA local quarantine or throttle is not proof that the emergency halt propagated across every required execution boundary."
                },
                {
                  "id": "AID-E-001",
                  "comparison": "AID-I-003 applies reversible quarantine, safe-mode downgrade, or throttling while investigation and recovery proceed; AID-E-001 authoritatively revokes compromised credentials, sessions, principals, issuance paths, and delegated grants after an incident decision.\nA quarantine receipt cannot prove durable identity-plane eviction, and revocation does not replace bounded containment of the affected workload or action."
                }
              ]
            },
